WEBVTT

00:00:02.140 --> 00:00:03.250
Huh?

00:00:04.600 --> 00:00:05.480
Um...

00:00:05.780 --> 00:00:06.860
Tsubasa.

00:00:07.730 --> 00:00:09.400
Tsubasa-chan, look this way!

00:00:09.400 --> 00:00:10.230
Huh?

00:00:10.230 --> 00:00:11.570
How do you feel?

00:00:11.570 --> 00:00:13.050
Can you show us some moves?

00:00:13.050 --> 00:00:14.130
Tell us more!

00:00:14.130 --> 00:00:15.500
Like I said!

00:00:15.500 --> 00:00:18.050
When you talk all at once, 
I can't answer anything!

00:00:18.050 --> 00:00:19.160
Tsubasa!

00:00:23.920 --> 00:00:25.370
So cool!

00:00:25.630 --> 00:00:26.800
No way!

00:00:30.010 --> 00:00:31.090
Hey, newbie!

00:00:31.270 --> 00:00:32.440
Newbie?!

00:00:32.440 --> 00:00:34.050
Y-You mean, me?

00:00:34.050 --> 00:00:37.130
You've become one of us now.

00:00:37.130 --> 00:00:38.680
Strive well!

00:00:41.690 --> 00:00:42.680
Okay!

00:00:42.680 --> 00:00:43.390
Good!

00:00:43.800 --> 00:00:45.440
Your mentor will be...

00:00:45.440 --> 00:00:46.850
you, Hajime!

00:00:46.850 --> 00:00:48.480
Oh, me?

00:00:48.480 --> 00:00:49.710
Roger!

00:00:49.710 --> 00:00:51.610
Tsubasa-chan, pleasure to work with you!

00:00:52.070 --> 00:00:54.790
Pleasure to work with you, Senpai!

00:02:25.350 --> 00:02:28.410
It's finally the Tachikawa 
mayoral elections tomorrow!

00:02:28.410 --> 00:02:31.330
<b>Vote with Your Thumb</b>

00:02:28.410 --> 00:02:31.330
<b>The First Smart Phone Elections in History! 
Tachikawa City Mayoral Elections</b>

00:02:28.830 --> 00:02:33.870
We're offering tips about 
the new smart phone election!

00:02:34.900 --> 00:02:37.130
If you don't have a tablet,

00:02:37.130 --> 00:02:38.920
we'll give you one for free

00:02:37.440 --> 00:02:38.270
Here.

00:02:38.920 --> 00:02:41.310
if you bring proof of residency!

00:02:40.240 --> 00:02:41.310
Here.

00:02:42.840 --> 00:02:44.350
I'm gloomy.

00:02:46.560 --> 00:02:47.830
Jou-san,

00:02:47.830 --> 00:02:50.600
can't you go a little slower?

00:02:50.910 --> 00:02:51.780
Sorry.

00:02:51.780 --> 00:02:54.520
Hey, teach us how, too!

00:02:55.020 --> 00:02:56.930
There's a voting app,

00:02:56.930 --> 00:02:58.860
so download that first.

00:02:58.860 --> 00:03:00.570
Hey, Sugane-kun.

00:03:00.570 --> 00:03:01.940
Is it true that you have a girlfriend?

00:03:01.940 --> 00:03:05.030
We heard it's one of your 
classmates in college.

00:03:05.030 --> 00:03:06.530
No, that's not true.

00:03:06.530 --> 00:03:08.580
Who started that rumor?

00:03:08.580 --> 00:03:10.040
Don't get too distracted, Sugane.

00:03:10.750 --> 00:03:11.590
Whoa!

00:03:11.590 --> 00:03:13.280
Sorry, Jou-san!

00:03:13.800 --> 00:03:18.510
<i>The Gatchaman have issued a statement 
about the mysterious alien</i>

00:03:18.510 --> 00:03:20.630
<i>who appeared in Nagaoka City, 
Niigata Prefecture!</i>

00:03:20.630 --> 00:03:22.970
<i>We have determined that Gelsadra</i>

00:03:22.970 --> 00:03:26.840
<i>is a harmless, peaceful life form!</i>

00:03:26.840 --> 00:03:29.660
On the contrary, planets where 
Sadra have taken up residence

00:03:29.660 --> 00:03:31.880
have been relieved of issues 
such as bullying, crime, war—

00:03:30.270 --> 00:03:39.150
<b>Live from Gatchannel</b>

00:03:33.150 --> 00:03:35.110
<i>Hey, don't cut in front of the camera!</i>

00:03:35.110 --> 00:03:39.390
<i>Uh... war, poverty, and so forth,</i>

00:03:39.390 --> 00:03:41.610
and some even report that 
they've achieved world peace!

00:03:40.650 --> 00:03:42.250
Oh, it's Pai-Pai.

00:03:42.250 --> 00:03:43.410
That's Pai-Pai-san to you.

00:03:43.410 --> 00:03:53.330
<b>Live from Gatchannel</b>

00:03:43.950 --> 00:03:46.400
<i>Of course we'll continue to monitor her,</i>

00:03:46.400 --> 00:03:50.390
<i>but we have high hopes that 
Gelsadra will prove to be a savior for Earth,</i>

00:03:50.390 --> 00:03:53.330
<i>which remains under protective observation!</i>

00:03:53.330 --> 00:03:55.500
What's a savior?

00:03:55.500 --> 00:03:57.420
Someone who'll save this planet!

00:03:57.420 --> 00:04:01.010
But in order for this planet 
to achieve true peace...

00:04:01.010 --> 00:04:02.880
we need

00:04:03.590 --> 00:04:05.050
your help.

00:04:05.050 --> 00:04:10.410
<b>Pai-Pai</b>

00:04:05.390 --> 00:04:10.430
<i>That's why I created Pai-Pai Daycare 
Center for the future of this planet...</i>

00:04:10.430 --> 00:04:15.650
<b>Live from Gatchannel</b>

00:04:12.370 --> 00:04:14.030
<i>Bite and Build!</i>

00:04:12.770 --> 00:04:15.650
<i>Hey! Stop it!</i>

00:04:15.650 --> 00:04:17.680
<b>Info-Live: The Millione Show</b>

00:04:15.650 --> 00:04:18.870
<i>The Millione Show!</i>

00:04:18.870 --> 00:04:19.610
<i>Hello!</i>

00:04:19.960 --> 00:04:22.320
<i>Welcome to Info-Live: The Millione Show!</i>

00:04:22.730 --> 00:04:25.220
<i>Well, yesterday was quite the surprise!</i>

00:04:25.220 --> 00:04:28.030
<i>A new Gatchaman was born 
right before the camera!</i>

00:04:28.370 --> 00:04:31.280
<i>And that tall JJ guy just came,</i>

00:04:31.280 --> 00:04:32.660
<i>Bam! out of nowhere!</i>

00:04:32.660 --> 00:04:34.950
<i>I was shocked, too!</i>

00:04:32.660 --> 00:04:37.410
<b>Celebration!! A New Gatchaman Member Is Born!! 
A Nagaoka Girl in High School: "Whoa, me?!"</b>

00:04:34.950 --> 00:04:37.420
<i>J stands out too much!</i>

00:04:37.420 --> 00:04:40.740
<i>So, this newest member— 
Misudachi Tsubasa-chan?</i>

00:04:40.740 --> 00:04:45.930
<i>They're going to have a send-off 
party for her at Riverside Senshuu.</i>

00:04:45.930 --> 00:04:49.770
<i>The Millione Show will have 
an exclusive live broadcast!</i>

00:04:49.770 --> 00:04:51.460
<i>Oh, this will be exciting!</i>

00:04:50.400 --> 00:04:52.140
A savior? Seriously?

00:04:52.140 --> 00:04:55.260
<i>It's great if we only had 
light topics like this,</i>

00:04:52.440 --> 00:04:54.190
Isn't Tsubasa-chan cute?

00:04:54.190 --> 00:04:55.640
She makes that sound.

00:04:55.260 --> 00:04:57.100
<i>but before we get into that...</i>

00:04:57.100 --> 00:04:59.750
<i>let's talk about the terrorist group, 
VAPE, who's all over the news these days!</i>

00:04:59.750 --> 00:05:03.390
<i>Today, we'll dig deep into the true 
identity of this fearsome group!</i>

00:05:04.020 --> 00:05:05.700
<i>Okay, here's what's up!</i>

00:05:05.110 --> 00:05:05.700
<b>In-Depth Analysis!</b>

00:05:05.110 --> 00:05:05.700
<b>What's VAPE?
 The Red CROWDS Organization</b>

00:05:05.700 --> 00:05:06.510
<b>In-Depth Analysis!</b>

00:05:05.700 --> 00:05:06.510
<b>What's VAPE?</b>

00:05:06.450 --> 00:05:08.080
<i>Yes, okay.</i>

00:05:06.510 --> 00:05:07.430
<b>The Red CROWDS Organization 
 Until now, CROWDS were only blue--why red now? 
 What are CROWDS, anyway?</b>

00:05:07.430 --> 00:05:08.660
<b>Materialized Human Consciousness</b>

00:05:07.430 --> 00:05:08.660
<b>They can materialize their consciousness anywhere in an instant 
 The users' thoughts appear on their faces, that look like a fuzzy LCD monitor 
 Use with <i>extreme</i> caution!</b>

00:05:08.660 --> 00:05:11.510
<i>Their consciousness? That's so hard!</i>

00:05:11.510 --> 00:05:13.250
<i>OD, is this right?</i>

00:05:13.250 --> 00:05:15.000
<i>Totally!</i>

00:05:15.000 --> 00:05:20.240
<i>So in other words, CROWDS are 
our thoughts and emotions given form.</i>

00:05:20.240 --> 00:05:24.510
<i>Even children and the elderly 
can use their smart phones</i>

00:05:24.510 --> 00:05:29.090
<i>to send their consciousness 
to a distant location.</i>

00:05:31.590 --> 00:05:34.400
<i>It is true that CROWDS 
have been very helpful</i>

00:05:34.400 --> 00:05:37.920
<i>in removing debris after 
the disaster and in volunteer work.</i>

00:05:37.920 --> 00:05:43.190
<i>But on the other hand, they've given rise 
to a dangerous organization like VAPE!</i>

00:05:44.030 --> 00:05:48.320
<i>And the one who's promoting the use 
of CROWDS as something anyone can do is...</i>

00:05:48.320 --> 00:05:49.060
<i>Him!</i>

00:05:49.500 --> 00:05:52.370
<i>Sugayama-san, is this really okay?</i>

00:05:52.370 --> 00:05:55.950
<i>Won't something terrible happen eventually?</i>

00:05:56.380 --> 00:05:58.870
X, what's the reaction on GALAX?

00:05:59.250 --> 00:06:01.190
Chaotic as usual.

00:06:01.630 --> 00:06:05.430
Critiques of CROWDS and Rui 
are growing by the day.

00:06:05.960 --> 00:06:10.250
Between the VAPE attack 
on the Prime Minister and now,

00:06:10.250 --> 00:06:15.980
53,684 users have uninstalled the CROWDS app.

00:06:16.390 --> 00:06:18.950
What about the mastermind 
behind the red CROWDS?

00:06:18.950 --> 00:06:21.420
Unfortunately, I have yet 
to identify who that is.

00:06:33.420 --> 00:06:35.620
It's nice to meet you, Ninomiya Rui-kun.

00:06:38.980 --> 00:06:40.930
Who are you?

00:06:41.740 --> 00:06:44.880
I am the one you most wish to see.

00:06:44.880 --> 00:06:47.370
You were able to come here using CROWDS.

00:06:47.370 --> 00:06:48.580
That means...

00:06:49.380 --> 00:06:51.140
I oversee VAPE.

00:06:52.470 --> 00:06:55.130
<b>Celebrate: The Newest Gatchaman Member! 
 Misudachi Tsubasa 
 Good luck, Star of Nagaoka!</b>

00:06:52.800 --> 00:06:55.140
Let's welcome them now!

00:06:55.140 --> 00:06:58.570
Misudachi Tsubasa-chan, 
the newest member of the Gatchaman!

00:06:58.570 --> 00:07:01.230
Ichinose Hajime-san, a Gatchaman!

00:07:01.490 --> 00:07:04.770
Gelsadra-kun, our special guest!

00:07:04.770 --> 00:07:05.750
Tsubasa!

00:07:05.750 --> 00:07:07.400
Gel-chan's so cute!

00:07:07.400 --> 00:07:08.990
It's Hajime-chan in the flesh!

00:07:08.990 --> 00:07:10.150
Look this way!

00:07:10.150 --> 00:07:11.570
She's blushing!

00:07:13.160 --> 00:07:14.340
Hello!

00:07:14.340 --> 00:07:16.550
I'm Misudachi Tsubasa!

00:07:16.550 --> 00:07:18.080
We know!

00:07:19.790 --> 00:07:21.080
Tsubasa!

00:07:19.790 --> 00:07:21.080
<b>Good Luck, Tsubasa!</b>

00:07:21.080 --> 00:07:22.480
Senpai!

00:07:22.480 --> 00:07:23.970
Thanks!

00:07:26.590 --> 00:07:27.480
Gatcha!

00:07:29.730 --> 00:07:32.030
Starting with "Gatcha!" 
right off the bat, huh?

00:07:32.030 --> 00:07:33.860
Tsubasa-chan, let's get right down to it.

00:07:33.860 --> 00:07:35.700
How do you feel now that you're a Gatchaman,

00:07:35.700 --> 00:07:36.970
<i>and what are your aspirations?</i>

00:07:36.970 --> 00:07:37.560
<i>Okay!</i>

00:07:38.040 --> 00:07:42.120
<i>Um... I became a Gatchaman 
really suddenly yesterday,</i>

00:07:42.120 --> 00:07:44.570
<i>and it still hasn't really sunk in.</i>

00:07:44.570 --> 00:07:46.620
<i>It's really weird.</i>

00:07:46.970 --> 00:07:49.070
<i>For now, I'm clueless 
about all this hero stuff</i>

00:07:49.070 --> 00:07:50.440
<i>and alien stuff to be honest,</i>

00:07:50.440 --> 00:07:53.230
<i>but I'm going to give it my very best shot</i>

00:07:53.230 --> 00:07:57.560
<i>and protect peace on Earth!</i>

00:08:01.900 --> 00:08:03.940
You're saying I'm wrong?

00:08:04.350 --> 00:08:07.490
There is a critical difference 
between you and I.

00:08:08.590 --> 00:08:12.070
I had feared my power and sealed it away.

00:08:12.630 --> 00:08:15.190
But you went ahead and used it right away.

00:08:15.190 --> 00:08:19.350
Furthermore, you shared 
that power with the general public.

00:08:19.350 --> 00:08:21.430
What's so wrong about that?

00:08:21.760 --> 00:08:24.160
Like I thought, you don't understand.

00:08:24.160 --> 00:08:25.150
Understand what?

00:08:25.380 --> 00:08:27.520
That the ones you gave this power to

00:08:27.520 --> 00:08:29.860
are apes who will never evolve.

00:08:30.610 --> 00:08:34.240
It means you are foolish for giving 
such a dangerous plaything

00:08:34.240 --> 00:08:35.860
to apes without any consideration.

00:08:36.240 --> 00:08:38.200
I'm not foolish.

00:08:38.730 --> 00:08:42.780
You're the ones who are 
using dangerous powers.

00:08:43.640 --> 00:08:45.330
That is all because of you.

00:08:45.790 --> 00:08:48.150
We are only trying to stop 
your idiotic actions,

00:08:48.150 --> 00:08:50.820
We are trying to make the apes understand

00:08:50.820 --> 00:08:55.800
just how dangerous it is to use CROWDS.

00:08:56.340 --> 00:08:58.030
How foolish.

00:08:58.030 --> 00:09:01.270
It's not. It is all for the sake of peace.

00:09:01.270 --> 00:09:02.320
Peace?

00:09:02.320 --> 00:09:05.350
You have no right to champion that word.

00:09:05.700 --> 00:09:08.110
You have a big misunderstanding.

00:09:08.470 --> 00:09:12.530
We are not the ones 
threatening this nation's peace.

00:09:13.020 --> 00:09:16.860
It is you, who gave his trust 
to the idiotic apes.

00:09:16.860 --> 00:09:18.070
Cut the bullshit!

00:09:18.070 --> 00:09:19.710
We're not apes.

00:09:19.710 --> 00:09:22.110
We are evolving, little by little.

00:09:22.110 --> 00:09:23.890
I'll never take the CROWDS away!

00:09:23.890 --> 00:09:25.780
I believe in everyone!

00:09:26.190 --> 00:09:29.670
Am I included among them?

00:09:29.670 --> 00:09:30.840
Of course.

00:09:30.840 --> 00:09:33.180
No matter what kind of person you might be,

00:09:33.180 --> 00:09:34.010
I'll never...

00:09:40.100 --> 00:09:41.340
Oh, my.

00:09:41.340 --> 00:09:42.890
It seems we are quite the apes, as well.

00:09:43.090 --> 00:09:44.390
Who are you?

00:09:44.710 --> 00:09:48.260
I am a radical peace activist.

00:10:13.360 --> 00:10:14.620
What's this?

00:10:14.620 --> 00:10:15.800
Bubbles?

00:10:16.020 --> 00:10:20.400
They seem to be everyone's feelings 
that Gel-chan has made visible!

00:10:20.400 --> 00:10:21.390
Feelings?!

00:10:26.110 --> 00:10:27.640
So cute!

00:10:27.640 --> 00:10:29.270
They're like speech bubbles in manga!

00:10:30.020 --> 00:10:31.730
Then we can call them bubbles-sama!

00:10:33.870 --> 00:10:35.600
Wow!

00:10:35.600 --> 00:10:38.860
Well, let's welcome the two Gatchaman!

00:10:38.860 --> 00:10:43.350
Today, we have a special treat: 
they'll transform for us!

00:10:43.350 --> 00:10:44.410
Tsubasa!

00:10:44.630 --> 00:10:46.470
Let's go, Tsubasa-chan!

00:10:46.470 --> 00:10:47.910
Got it!

00:10:47.910 --> 00:10:51.120
Go, Bird!

00:10:58.030 --> 00:10:58.800
Huh?

00:10:58.800 --> 00:10:59.870
Why?

00:11:00.700 --> 00:11:02.210
You're still Tsubasa!

00:11:04.960 --> 00:11:06.190
Right.

00:11:07.720 --> 00:11:08.480
Go!

00:11:08.480 --> 00:11:11.030
Maybe you're a bit nervous?

00:11:11.430 --> 00:11:12.730
Want to give it another try?

00:11:12.730 --> 00:11:13.910
Okay!

00:11:13.910 --> 00:11:16.210
Go, Bird!

00:11:16.870 --> 00:11:18.710
Tsubasa-chan, you do it like this.

00:11:18.710 --> 00:11:19.960
Like this?

00:11:19.960 --> 00:11:21.940
Like this, and this!

00:11:21.940 --> 00:11:24.060
Like this, and this?

00:11:41.770 --> 00:11:42.800
I understand now...

00:11:44.080 --> 00:11:46.180
Gatchaman have it really hard.

00:11:46.390 --> 00:11:47.010
What?

00:11:53.500 --> 00:11:55.100
But Tsubasa-chan,

00:11:55.520 --> 00:11:57.550
you work hard,

00:11:57.550 --> 00:11:59.410
so I think you can get this down!

00:12:00.160 --> 00:12:02.360
Thank you, Gel-chan!

00:12:08.860 --> 00:12:11.290
Kill the CROWDS.

00:12:17.300 --> 00:12:18.130
What the?

00:12:19.740 --> 00:12:20.920
Huh? No way...

00:12:24.270 --> 00:12:26.120
I'm going for a bit!

00:12:26.120 --> 00:12:29.230
Tsubasa-chan, please evacuate 
the audience outside!

00:12:29.230 --> 00:12:31.000
No, I'll go, too!

00:12:31.000 --> 00:12:32.650
I'll be fine!

00:12:33.310 --> 00:12:34.310
Senpai!

00:12:46.580 --> 00:12:48.450
Rui, we have an emergency.

00:12:48.780 --> 00:12:52.790
Red CROWDS have appeared at Riverside 
Senshuu in Nagaoka City, Niigata Prefecture.

00:12:52.790 --> 00:12:53.720
Hajime!

00:12:53.720 --> 00:12:55.390
Be careful of their attacks!

00:12:55.390 --> 00:12:57.170
Good luck, Hajime-chan!

00:12:57.430 --> 00:12:59.750
I know, Pai-Pai!

00:13:18.400 --> 00:13:20.440
Yeah! Party time!

00:13:20.830 --> 00:13:22.500
Rizumin, go!

00:13:22.500 --> 00:13:25.780
Hajime-tan, I wanna join in, too!

00:13:25.780 --> 00:13:28.620
Katze-san, good night.

00:13:30.080 --> 00:13:32.860
Meanie!

00:13:33.580 --> 00:13:34.460
Sparkle!

00:13:34.700 --> 00:13:37.630
Everyone, the emergency exit is this way!

00:13:39.800 --> 00:13:43.070
Newbie, stay calm and 
help evacuate everyone!

00:13:43.070 --> 00:13:44.330
Got it!

00:13:44.330 --> 00:13:46.180
Everyone, please calm down!

00:13:47.780 --> 00:13:48.930
Those bastards!

00:13:49.310 --> 00:13:51.970
Go, Bird!

00:13:53.570 --> 00:13:55.430
Oh, c'mon!

00:13:55.910 --> 00:13:56.940
Go!

00:13:56.940 --> 00:13:57.900
Go!

00:13:57.900 --> 00:13:59.140
Go!

00:13:59.420 --> 00:14:00.940
Ugh!

00:14:01.340 --> 00:14:04.360
We have a <i>situation</i>!

00:14:04.360 --> 00:14:05.940
Isn't this bad?

00:14:05.940 --> 00:14:07.450
Everyone's a hero, right?

00:14:07.450 --> 00:14:08.660
Here we go!

00:14:09.670 --> 00:14:10.570
Let's go!

00:14:18.160 --> 00:14:18.930
What?

00:14:18.930 --> 00:14:20.200
We have blue ones now?

00:14:20.680 --> 00:14:21.920
Seriously?

00:14:22.300 --> 00:14:23.250
Stop...

00:14:23.600 --> 00:14:24.760
Everyone stop.

00:14:24.760 --> 00:14:27.860
<i>We have a battle between 
the blue and red CROWDS!</i>

00:14:27.860 --> 00:14:29.560
<i>It's like a war!</i>

00:14:29.560 --> 00:14:32.840
<i>Uh, oh! You're all way too excited!</i>

00:14:30.060 --> 00:14:31.540
A war!

00:14:33.310 --> 00:14:34.770
Hey, stop!

00:14:37.820 --> 00:14:39.480
This is a civil war.

00:14:39.480 --> 00:14:42.150
I always thought CROWDS were dangerous.

00:14:42.420 --> 00:14:44.110
Rui, what would you like to do?

00:14:44.760 --> 00:14:45.590
Rui?

